From 2fff41c9560dc377b1a4b665fa81e15d3ddb739a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 17:28:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] [rh2-integration] close pre-rental audit evidence gaps in the
 event layer

rh2 pre-rental full audit (codex_miles_prerental_full_audit_20260828.md)
found the G1 acceptance evidence layer could green-light runs whose
training facts were wrong. This commit closes the emitter-side gaps; the
collector/judge counterparts live in rh2.

- PR-P0-1: every event carries run_id when MILES_RH2_RUN_ID is set, so a
  collector can reject events leaked from another run in a shared dir.
- PR-P0-7: train_step_consumed attributes samples to optimizer steps via
  the DataIterator's real micro-batch schedule (micro_batch_indices +
  per-step num_microbatches, or fixed micro_batch_size slices) through
  the new pure helper miles/utils/step_attribution.py. The old equal
  split silently mis-attributed samples under variable fan-out (3/1
  local rows were booked as 2/2).
- PR-P0-5: narrow trainer-side R3 replay evidence: replay_fill (stream
  count, records vs expected, per-sample converted-tape digests that
  hash-match the rollout_group source digests), replay_consume (per
  logprob forward pass and per optimizer step, min/max pop deltas), and
  replay_exhausted (end-of-rollout drain) via
  BaseReplayManager.consumption_snapshot. No algorithm change.
- PR-P0-3A: eval_smoke now carries weight_version, so a pre-train eval
  can no longer impersonate the post-train eval.
- PR-P0-8: logprob_compare entries (miles/utils/logprob_compare.py)
  count only loss_mask==1 provenance tokens and preserve length
  mismatches as facts instead of truncating; train forward_step ships
  sample_indices so a custom loss can attribute accepted-token facts.
- PR-P1-2: independent zero_signal_scan_seconds timing on train_step.

Everything stays no-op unless MILES_RH2_EVENT_DIR is set.
